---
const stops = [
  {
    era: "1940s–50s",
    title: "Bradbury prose + EC comics",
    detail: "Compact stories become illustrated shocks.",
  },
  {
    era: "1954–55",
    title: "Comics Code disruption",
    detail: "The market closes around EC horror.",
  },
  {
    era: "1982",
    title: "Creepshow",
    detail: "Panels, colors, effects, and punchlines move into film.",
  },
  {
    era: "1985–92",
    title: "Ray Bradbury Theater",
    detail: "An author’s archive becomes hosted anthology television.",
  },
  {
    era: "1989–96",
    title: "Tales from the Crypt",
    detail: "HBO reopens the EC library for filmmakers.",
  },
  {
    era: "Now",
    title: "Independent horror",
    detail: "Smaller cameras lower the floor without removing the work.",
  },
];
---

<figure class="story-containers not-prose" aria-labelledby="story-containers-title">
  <div class="heading">
    <p>The form keeps moving</p>
    <h2 id="story-containers-title">Stories change containers</h2>
  </div>

  <ol>
    {stops.map((stop) => (
      <li>
        <span class="era">{stop.era}</span>
        <h3>{stop.title}</h3>
        <p>{stop.detail}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <figcaption>
    This is a route through overlapping people and forms, not a claim that every stop caused the next one.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .story-containers {
    margin: 3rem 0;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    color: #211b17;
    background:
      linear-gradient(rgb(84 44 29 / 0.07) 1px, transparent 1px),
      #e6d7af;
    background-size: 100% 1.45rem;
    border: 1px solid #7d5d39;
    box-shadow: 0.45rem 0.55rem 0 #2f2924;
  }

  .heading p,
  .heading h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .heading p {
    color: #7c3128;
    font: 800 0.72rem/1.2 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .heading h2 {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    font: 900 clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.7rem)/1 Georgia, serif;
  }

  ol {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  li {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 9.25rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.35rem 1rem 1rem;
    border-top: 3px solid #2b6d67;
    border-right: 1px dashed rgb(57 45 34 / 0.36);
  }

  li:nth-child(2),
  li:nth-child(5) {
    border-top-color: #9b3228;
  }

  li:nth-child(3),
  li:nth-child(6) {
    border-top-color: #28231f;
  }

  li::before {
    position: absolute;
    top: -0.55rem;
    left: 0;
    width: 0.85rem;
    height: 0.85rem;
    background: #e6d7af;
    border: 3px solid currentColor;
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: inherit;
    content: "";
  }

  .era {
    color: #7c3128;
    font: 800 0.68rem/1.2 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0.45rem 0;
    font: 800 1rem/1.05 Georgia, serif;
  }

  li p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #55493e;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  figcaption {
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
    color: #55493e;
    border-top: 1px solid rgb(57 45 34 / 0.3);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    ol {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    ol {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    li {
      min-height: 0;
      border-right: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
